// Lesson 6.1 — Gravity & Jump: The First Flick
// Unit 6 opens in the cave. Nothing in the starter jumps: PlayerController.cs is
// the student's own file from 1.4 onward, and the Rigidbody2D built in 2.1 was
// tuned for a top-down world with Gravity Scale 0. So this lesson is two new
// mechanisms, and at level 1 each gets its own walkthrough: turning gravity on
// for ONE scene, and the flick that leaves the ground.
//
// GROUND TRUTH (verified against the teacher's finished project):
//   - Unity 6000.6.0f1. Legacy Input class, so Input.GetKeyDown is correct.
//     Rigidbody2D.linearVelocity, not the old `velocity`.
//   - The build decides "which world am I in" by SCENE NAME in Start():
//     SceneManager.GetActiveScene().name == "Overworld". isPlatformer is a
//     plain private field - NOT [SerializeField]. There is no Inspector tick,
//     and the old inert `isPlatformer: 1` override has been removed from
//     Platformer.unity precisely so nobody goes looking for it.
//   - The body reference is named `rb`, not `body`.
//   - The jump key is J, the field is [SerializeField] float jumpForce (the
//     Platformer scene overrides it to 10), and the push is
//     rb.AddForceY(jumpForce, ForceMode2D.Impulse) - AddForceY, not
//     AddForce(Vector2.up * ...).
//   - The build prints "jump" in Jump(). It does NOT print vertical velocity.
//   - EditorBuildSettings orders the scenes Start(0), Overworld(1), Platformer(2)
//     — "the cave is index 2" is real, and SceneSwitch.cs holds a serialized int
//     build index, not a name.
//   - Physics2DSettings ships m_Gravity {x: 0, y: -9.81}, so Gravity Scale really
//     is a multiplier on it.
//   - Player.prefab: root Transform + PlayerController; the SpriteRenderer and
//     Animator live on a child called `Sprite`. No Rigidbody2D and no Collider2D
//     in the shipped starter — those are the student's work from 2.1.
//   - Do not call the cave's ground body "Gravity Scale 0" — the Collision tilemap
//     is a Static body whose Inspector reads Gravity Scale 1, greyed out.
//   - SceneSwitch.cs really does switch scenes from OnCollisionEnter2D, so the
//     Kinematic row of the technique table is right that a Kinematic Player would
//     make the cave door go silent.
//
// SCOPE: this lesson stops at "the character can leave the ground". It does NOT
// add jumpsRemaining - unlimited mid-air jumps are the discovery that opens 6.2,
// and teaching the fix here would leave 6.2 with nothing to do. The reference
// project has the fix because the reference project is the end of the story.
//
// PROTECTED BLOCKS - ids are POSITIONAL. socratic "Gravity Is a Number You Own"
// is the FIRST socratic in the document and stays first, in that order, three
// <li> so its ids stay 6.1:sc1:q1..q3. dc1:q1..q2 are unchanged in count.
